IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `cpr-dates`
IMPORT `cpr-claims`

-- Court Procedures Rules 2006 (ACT) -- worked cases for the questions of the person bringing a claim.
--
-- Every assertion is a claim about the ENCODING on stated facts, not about the law. Expected values were written by hand
-- from the text before the file was run; none was copied from the encoding's output. All facts are HYPOTHETICAL.
--
-- (c) Australian Capital Territory. Used under CC BY 4.0 (SOURCE-LICENSE.md). Unofficial text.
-- BASELINE ENCODING. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Short names`

GIVEN d IS A NUMBER, m IS A NUMBER, y IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DATE
`on` d m y MEANS `the calendar date` d m y

`any day` MEANS `on` 1 1 2000

`SC` MEANS `the Supreme Court`
`MC` MEANS `the Magistrates Court`

`VALID` MEANS `yes: the originating process is still valid for service (r 74 (1))`
`VALID RENEWED` MEANS `yes: the originating process is valid for service under the renewal the court gave (r 74 (3))`
`NOT VALID` MEANS `no: the originating process is no longer valid for service (r 74 (1)); you may apply to renew it even now (r 74 (4)), or start a fresh proceeding (r 74 (7))`

`DISMISSED 1A` MEANS `taken to be dismissed against the defendant: no affidavit of service was filed within 1 year after the originating process was issued (r 75 (1) (a)); you must pay the defendant's costs (r 75 (5)) unless the court reinstates it (r 76)`
`DISMISSED 1B` MEANS `taken to be dismissed against the defendant: the defendant filed nothing, and no judgment was entered, within 1 year after service (r 75 (1) (b)); you must pay the defendant's costs (r 75 (5)) unless the court reinstates it (r 76)`
`DISMISSED 2` MEANS `taken to be dismissed: no step was taken within 1 year after the last step (r 75 (2)); a party filing a document within 1 year after the dismissal reinstates it (r 76 (3)), or the court may (r 76 (2))`
`REINSTATED` MEANS `dismissed under r 75 (2), but reinstated by a document filed within 1 year after the dismissal (r 76 (3)); for any time limit it is taken never to have been dismissed (r 76 (5))`
`NOT DISMISSED` MEANS `not taken to be dismissed on these facts (r 75: none of its conditions is met at this day)`

`MC YES` MEANS `yes, for at most $250 000, if you abandon the excess and say so in the claim; the judgment discharges the whole cause of action (r 55)`
`MC NO` MEANS `not under r 55: it lets you sue in the Magistrates Court only if you abandon the excess and state that in the claim (the text's no)`
`MC NA` MEANS `r 55 does not apply: the cause of action is not for more than $250 000; whether the Magistrates Court can hear it is a question for the Magistrates Court Act 1930, not these rules (NOTHING-kind)`

`NO CONDITIONAL` MEANS `no conditional notice of intention to respond was filed`
`CONDITIONAL LAPSED` MEANS `a conditional notice was filed and no application under rule 40 followed within 28 days`
`CONDITIONAL REFUSED` MEANS `a conditional notice was filed and the defendant's application under rule 40 was refused`

`IN DEFAULT` MEANS `yes: the defendant is in default (r 1117 (1)); you may apply for default judgment and carry on against any other party (r 1118 (1))`
`STRUCK OUT` MEANS `yes: the defence was struck out, so the defendant is in default (r 1117 (1) (a) (iv)); you may apply for default judgment (r 1118 (1))`
`NOT YET` MEANS `not yet: the time for the defence has not ended (r 1117 (1) not met)`
`IN TIME` MEANS `no: the defence was filed in time (r 1117 (1) not met)`
`LATE BEFORE DJ` MEANS `no: the defence was filed late but before default judgment, so the defendant is not in default (r 1117 (2) (a) (iii))`
`STAYED` MEANS `no: the proceeding is stayed because the defendant paid what was claimed (r 1117 (2) (a) (i), r 1102)`
`ACKNOWLEDGED` MEANS `no: the defendant has filed an acknowledgment of the debt or liquidated demand (r 1117 (2) (a) (ii), r 1104)`
`NOT ORIGINATING CLAIM` MEANS `division 2.11.3 does not apply: the proceeding was not started by originating claim (r 1116) (NOTHING-kind)`

`DJ 1120` MEANS `r 1120: judgment for not more than the amount claimed, with the interest and costs stated in the affidavit in support (or costs to be agreed or assessed)`
`DJ 1122` MEANS `r 1122: judgment for damages to be assessed (with or without your other claims); r 1126 is then not open for the other claims`
`DJ 1123` MEANS `r 1123: judgment for the return of the goods or their value, or their value, with costs`
`DJ 1124` MEANS `r 1124: judgment for possession of the land, with the costs of the claim and of getting judgment`
`DJ 1125` MEANS `r 1125: judgment on all or any of your claims, each as if it were your only claim under r 1120, r 1123 or r 1124`
`DJ 1126` MEANS `r 1126: the judgment the court considers justified on your claim, after a hearing on application with the relevant affidavits`
`DJ NONE` MEANS `no claim for relief was stated`

`1725 NA` MEANS `r 1725 does not apply: the judgment is not one it covers; your costs follow the ordinary rules (NOTHING-kind)`
`1725 B` MEANS `the Magistrates Court determined fee, and 50% of the disbursements (not the costs) you could have recovered in the Supreme Court on a judgment over $250 000 (r 1725 (2) (a), (b))`
`1725 C` MEANS `the Magistrates Court determined fee, and 50% of the costs and disbursements you could have recovered in the Supreme Court on a judgment over $250 000 (r 1725 (2) (a), (c))`
`1725 D` MEANS `the Magistrates Court determined fee, and 75% of the costs and disbursements you could have recovered in the Supreme Court on a judgment over $250 000 (r 1725 (2) (a), (d))`
`1725 ORDERED` MEANS `the amount the court ordered instead (r 1725 (3))`

`ME` MEANS `I made the offer`
`DEF` MEANS `the defendant made the offer`
`ACCEPTED` MEANS `the offer was accepted`
`FOR ME` MEANS `judgment for me`
`FOR DEF` MEANS `judgment for the defendant, or my claim dismissed`
`1009 P` MEANS `r 1009 (2): you get your costs from the defendant, party and party, up to the time the offer was made`
`1009 D` MEANS `r 1009 (3): the defendant gets its costs from you, party and party, up to the time the offer was made`
`1010 A` MEANS `r 1010 (2) (a): you get your costs from the defendant on a solicitor and client basis for the whole proceeding (personal injury claim)`
`1010 B` MEANS `r 1010 (2) (b): you get your costs from the defendant, party and party until the switch day, and solicitor and client from it`
`1011 A` MEANS `r 1011 (2) (a): you get your costs, party and party, up to and including the day of the offer, and none after; you pay none of the defendant's costs from that day (personal injury claim)`
`1011 B` MEANS `r 1011 (2) (b): you get your costs, party and party, until the switch day; from it the defendant gets its costs from you, party and party`
`1012` MEANS `r 1012: the defendant gets its costs from you, party and party until the switch day, and solicitor and client from it`
`NO OFFER ORDER` MEANS `Part 2.10 gives no costs order on these facts: the offer made provision for costs, or the judgment did not meet the offer, or the offeror was not shown willing and able (r 1014 (3)); costs follow the ordinary rules (NOTHING-kind)`
`OFFER ORDERED OTHERWISE` MEANS `the court ordered otherwise: Part 2.10's costs rule gives way to its order (NOTHING-kind)`

`SWITCH 1010 1011` MEANS `r 1010 or r 1011 (judgment for me)`
`SWITCH 1012` MEANS `r 1012 (judgment for the defendant)`

`NO LATER INTEREST` MEANS `no: the offer was an appropriate settlement amount (r 1619 (8)), so the court must not order interest for the period after it (r 1619 (7))`
`SPECIAL` MEANS `yes, the court may: the offer was an appropriate settlement amount, but the special circumstances of the case justify interest after it (r 1619 (7))`
`NOT SETTLED` MEANS `r 1619 (8) does not settle it: the judgment exceeds the offer by more than 10%; whether the offer was still an appropriate settlement amount is not said (NOTHING-kind)`
`NO OFFER` MEANS `r 1619 (7) does not bar it: the defendant made no settlement offer`
`NOT DAMAGES` MEANS `r 1619 (7) does not apply: not a proceeding for damages (NOTHING-kind)`

`NO JUDGMENT INTEREST` MEANS `none: the judgment was paid in full within 28 days after it took effect (r 1620 (2))`
`JUDGMENT INTEREST NOT YET` MEANS `not yet decided: the 28 days have not ended and the judgment is not paid in full (r 1620 (2))`
`JUDGMENT INTEREST` MEANS `yes: interest is payable on the unpaid amount at the schedule 2, part 2.2 rate (or the rate in your claim, after a r 1120 default judgment) (r 1620 (1))`
`JUDGMENT INTEREST ORDERED` MEANS `the court ordered otherwise: r 1620 gives way to its order (NOTHING-kind)`

`UP TO` MEANS `interest up to judgment`
`AFTER` MEANS `interest after judgment`

`PR` MEANS `the deceased person's personal representative`
`FAMILY` MEANS `a member of the deceased person's family who suffered damage or loss because of the death`
`OTHER PERSON` MEANS `someone else`
`PR STARTS` MEANS `yes: the personal representative starts the proceeding, for the family members who suffered loss (r 250 (2))`
`FAMILY MAY` MEANS `yes: the personal representative did not start it within 6 months after the death, so you may, for the same people (r 250 (3), (4))`
`FAMILY NOT YET` MEANS `not yet: within 6 months after the death only the personal representative may start it (r 250 (2), (3))`
`ONLY ONE` MEANS `no: a proceeding has already been started against this person for this death; only one may be (r 250 (1)); ask the court to add a name left out (r 251)`
`NOT YOU` MEANS `no: only the personal representative or, after 6 months, a family member who suffered loss may start it (r 250 (2), (3))`

§ `The date helpers`

-- 31 August + 6 months: no 31 February; the last day of February (2028 is a leap year).
#ASSERT (`on` 31 8 2027) `plus months` 6 EQUALS `on` 29 2 2028
-- 28 counted days from 20 December 2026: 21-24 December (4), then 2-25 January (24), skipping 25 December - 1 January.
#ASSERT (`on` 20 12 2026) `plus counted days` 28 EQUALS `on` 25 1 2027
#ASSERT (`on` 1 3 2026) `plus counted days` 28 EQUALS `on` 29 3 2026

§ `r 32 -- the day the proceeding started`

#ASSERT `r 32 -- on what day did my proceeding start` FALSE (`on` 3 3 2026) `any day` EQUALS `on` 3 3 2026
#ASSERT `r 32 -- on what day did my proceeding start` TRUE (`on` 3 3 2026) (`on` 1 2 2026) EQUALS `on` 1 2 2026

§ `r 74 -- validity and renewal`

-- Filed 1 March 2026: 1 year starting that day ends 28 February 2027.
#ASSERT `r 74 (1) -- the last day of the first year of validity` (`on` 1 3 2026) EQUALS `on` 28 2 2027
#ASSERT `r 74 (1) -- the last day of the first year of validity` (`on` 15 6 2026) EQUALS `on` 14 6 2027
-- Filed 29 February 2024: ends 28 February 2025. Filed 1 March 2024: also ends 28 February 2025 (fork F3).
#ASSERT `r 74 (1) -- the last day of the first year of validity` (`on` 29 2 2024) EQUALS `on` 28 2 2025
#ASSERT `r 74 (1) -- the last day of the first year of validity` (`on` 1 3 2024) EQUALS `on` 28 2 2025

#ASSERT `r 74 -- can I still serve my originating process` (`on` 1 3 2026) FALSE `any day` (`on` 28 2 2027) EQUALS `VALID`
#ASSERT `r 74 -- can I still serve my originating process` (`on` 1 3 2026) FALSE `any day` (`on` 1 3 2027) EQUALS `NOT VALID`
#ASSERT `r 74 -- can I still serve my originating process` (`on` 1 3 2026) TRUE (`on` 28 8 2027) (`on` 28 8 2027) EQUALS `VALID RENEWED`
#ASSERT `r 74 -- can I still serve my originating process` (`on` 1 3 2026) TRUE (`on` 28 8 2027) (`on` 29 8 2027) EQUALS `NOT VALID`
-- Within the first year, the first-year answer comes first even if renewed.
#ASSERT `r 74 -- can I still serve my originating process` (`on` 1 3 2026) TRUE (`on` 28 8 2027) (`on` 1 1 2027) EQUALS `VALID`

#ASSERT `r 74 (3) -- the latest day one renewal can run to` (`on` 28 2 2027) EQUALS `on` 28 8 2027
#ASSERT `r 74 (3) -- the latest day one renewal can run to` (`on` 31 8 2027) EQUALS `on` 29 2 2028
#ASSERT `r 74 (3) -- the latest day one renewal can run to` (`on` 31 8 2026) EQUALS `on` 28 2 2027

§ `r 75, r 76 (3) -- dismissal for delay`

-- The rule's own example: last step 1 July 2006, dismissed 2 July 2007.
#ASSERT `r 75 (4) -- the day my proceeding would be dismissed for want of a step` (`on` 1 7 2006) EQUALS `on` 2 7 2007
-- Last step 29 February 2024: the year ends 28 February 2025; dismissed 1 March 2025 (fork F3).
#ASSERT `r 75 (4) -- the day my proceeding would be dismissed for want of a step` (`on` 29 2 2024) EQUALS `on` 1 3 2025

-- Issued 1 March 2026, affidavit of service 10 March 2026, served 5 March 2026, defence 20 March 2026, last step
-- 1 June 2026. The year after the last step ends 1 June 2027; dismissed 2 June 2027.
#ASSERT `r 75 -- is my proceeding taken to be dismissed` (`on` 1 3 2026) TRUE (`on` 10 3 2026) TRUE (`on` 5 3 2026) TRUE (`on` 20 3 2026) FALSE `any day` (`on` 1 6 2026) FALSE `any day` (`on` 1 6 2027) EQUALS `NOT DISMISSED`
#ASSERT `r 75 -- is my proceeding taken to be dismissed` (`on` 1 3 2026) TRUE (`on` 10 3 2026) TRUE (`on` 5 3 2026) TRUE (`on` 20 3 2026) FALSE `any day` (`on` 1 6 2026) FALSE `any day` (`on` 2 6 2027) EQUALS `DISMISSED 2`
-- Dismissed 2 June 2027; a document filed by 2 June 2028 reinstates it; one filed 3 June 2028 does not.
#ASSERT `r 75 -- is my proceeding taken to be dismissed` (`on` 1 3 2026) TRUE (`on` 10 3 2026) TRUE (`on` 5 3 2026) TRUE (`on` 20 3 2026) FALSE `any day` (`on` 1 6 2026) TRUE (`on` 1 6 2028) (`on` 3 6 2028) EQUALS `REINSTATED`
#ASSERT `r 75 -- is my proceeding taken to be dismissed` (`on` 1 3 2026) TRUE (`on` 10 3 2026) TRUE (`on` 5 3 2026) TRUE (`on` 20 3 2026) FALSE `any day` (`on` 1 6 2026) TRUE (`on` 2 6 2028) (`on` 3 6 2028) EQUALS `REINSTATED`
#ASSERT `r 75 -- is my proceeding taken to be dismissed` (`on` 1 3 2026) TRUE (`on` 10 3 2026) TRUE (`on` 5 3 2026) TRUE (`on` 20 3 2026) FALSE `any day` (`on` 1 6 2026) TRUE (`on` 3 6 2028) (`on` 4 6 2028) EQUALS `DISMISSED 2`
-- r 75 (1) (a): no affidavit of service; the year after issue ends 1 March 2027.
#ASSERT `r 75 -- is my proceeding taken to be dismissed` (`on` 1 3 2026) FALSE `any day` TRUE (`on` 5 3 2026) TRUE (`on` 20 3 2026) FALSE `any day` (`on` 1 6 2026) FALSE `any day` (`on` 1 3 2027) EQUALS `NOT DISMISSED`
#ASSERT `r 75 -- is my proceeding taken to be dismissed` (`on` 1 3 2026) FALSE `any day` TRUE (`on` 5 3 2026) TRUE (`on` 20 3 2026) FALSE `any day` (`on` 1 6 2026) FALSE `any day` (`on` 2 3 2027) EQUALS `DISMISSED 1A`
-- An affidavit filed the day after the year ended comes too late (finding 5: even though the defendant has a defence in).
#ASSERT `r 75 -- is my proceeding taken to be dismissed` (`on` 1 3 2026) TRUE (`on` 2 3 2027) TRUE (`on` 5 3 2026) TRUE (`on` 20 3 2026) FALSE `any day` (`on` 1 6 2026) FALSE `any day` (`on` 3 3 2027) EQUALS `DISMISSED 1A`
-- r 75 (1) (b): served 5 March 2026, no response; the year after service ends 5 March 2027. Last step 10 March 2026.
#ASSERT `r 75 -- is my proceeding taken to be dismissed` (`on` 1 3 2026) TRUE (`on` 10 3 2026) TRUE (`on` 5 3 2026) FALSE `any day` FALSE `any day` (`on` 10 3 2026) FALSE `any day` (`on` 5 3 2027) EQUALS `NOT DISMISSED`
#ASSERT `r 75 -- is my proceeding taken to be dismissed` (`on` 1 3 2026) TRUE (`on` 10 3 2026) TRUE (`on` 5 3 2026) FALSE `any day` FALSE `any day` (`on` 10 3 2026) FALSE `any day` (`on` 6 3 2027) EQUALS `DISMISSED 1B`
#ASSERT `r 75 -- is my proceeding taken to be dismissed` (`on` 1 3 2026) TRUE (`on` 10 3 2026) TRUE (`on` 5 3 2026) FALSE `any day` TRUE (`on` 1 2 2027) (`on` 10 3 2026) FALSE `any day` (`on` 6 3 2027) EQUALS `NOT DISMISSED`
#ASSERT `r 75 -- is my proceeding taken to be dismissed` (`on` 1 3 2026) TRUE (`on` 10 3 2026) TRUE (`on` 5 3 2026) TRUE (`on` 6 3 2027) FALSE `any day` (`on` 10 3 2026) FALSE `any day` (`on` 7 3 2027) EQUALS `DISMISSED 1B`

§ `r 55 -- abandoning the excess`

#ASSERT `r 55 -- can I sue in the Magistrates Court by abandoning the excess` 300000 TRUE EQUALS `MC YES`
#ASSERT `r 55 -- can I sue in the Magistrates Court by abandoning the excess` 300000 FALSE EQUALS `MC NO`
#ASSERT `r 55 -- can I sue in the Magistrates Court by abandoning the excess` 250000 TRUE EQUALS `MC NA`
#ASSERT `r 55 -- can I sue in the Magistrates Court by abandoning the excess` 250001 TRUE EQUALS `MC YES`

§ `r 102, r 111 -- the defendant's last day for a defence`

-- Served 1 March 2026: 28 days after is 29 March 2026.
#ASSERT `r 102 -- by what day must the defendant file a defence` (`on` 1 3 2026) `NO CONDITIONAL` `any day` FALSE `any day` EQUALS `on` 29 3 2026
-- Served 10 December 2026: 11-24 December (14), then 2-15 January (14), skipping 25 December - 1 January.
#ASSERT `r 102 -- by what day must the defendant file a defence` (`on` 10 12 2026) `NO CONDITIONAL` `any day` FALSE `any day` EQUALS `on` 15 1 2027
-- r 40 application refused 25 March 2026: 7 days is 1 April, later than 29 March.
#ASSERT `r 102 -- by what day must the defendant file a defence` (`on` 1 3 2026) `NO CONDITIONAL` `any day` TRUE (`on` 25 3 2026) EQUALS `on` 1 4 2026
-- Refused 10 March 2026: 7 days is 17 March; 29 March is later.
#ASSERT `r 102 -- by what day must the defendant file a defence` (`on` 1 3 2026) `NO CONDITIONAL` `any day` TRUE (`on` 10 3 2026) EQUALS `on` 29 3 2026
-- Conditional notice filed 5 March 2026, no application: 28 days end 2 April; unconditional 3 April; 14 days: 17 April.
#ASSERT `r 102 -- by what day must the defendant file a defence` (`on` 1 3 2026) `CONDITIONAL LAPSED` (`on` 5 3 2026) FALSE `any day` EQUALS `on` 17 4 2026
-- Conditional notice, application refused 20 March 2026: unconditional that day; 14 days: 3 April (r 111 (5), fork F7).
#ASSERT `r 102 -- by what day must the defendant file a defence` (`on` 1 3 2026) `CONDITIONAL REFUSED` (`on` 2 3 2026) TRUE (`on` 20 3 2026) EQUALS `on` 3 4 2026

§ `r 1117 -- is the defendant in default`

-- Served 1 March 2026; last day 29 March 2026.
#ASSERT `r 1117 -- is the defendant in default` TRUE (`on` 1 3 2026) `NO CONDITIONAL` `any day` FALSE `any day` FALSE `any day` FALSE `any day` FALSE FALSE FALSE (`on` 29 3 2026) EQUALS `NOT YET`
#ASSERT `r 1117 -- is the defendant in default` TRUE (`on` 1 3 2026) `NO CONDITIONAL` `any day` FALSE `any day` FALSE `any day` FALSE `any day` FALSE FALSE FALSE (`on` 30 3 2026) EQUALS `IN DEFAULT`
#ASSERT `r 1117 -- is the defendant in default` TRUE (`on` 1 3 2026) `NO CONDITIONAL` `any day` FALSE `any day` FALSE `any day` TRUE (`on` 29 3 2026) FALSE FALSE FALSE (`on` 10 4 2026) EQUALS `IN TIME`
#ASSERT `r 1117 -- is the defendant in default` TRUE (`on` 1 3 2026) `NO CONDITIONAL` `any day` FALSE `any day` FALSE `any day` TRUE (`on` 5 4 2026) FALSE FALSE FALSE (`on` 10 4 2026) EQUALS `LATE BEFORE DJ`
-- A defence dated after the day asked about has not been filed yet.
#ASSERT `r 1117 -- is the defendant in default` TRUE (`on` 1 3 2026) `NO CONDITIONAL` `any day` FALSE `any day` FALSE `any day` TRUE (`on` 15 4 2026) FALSE FALSE FALSE (`on` 10 4 2026) EQUALS `IN DEFAULT`
-- A further period agreed to 20 April 2026.
#ASSERT `r 1117 -- is the defendant in default` TRUE (`on` 1 3 2026) `NO CONDITIONAL` `any day` FALSE `any day` TRUE (`on` 20 4 2026) FALSE `any day` FALSE FALSE FALSE (`on` 20 4 2026) EQUALS `NOT YET`
#ASSERT `r 1117 -- is the defendant in default` TRUE (`on` 1 3 2026) `NO CONDITIONAL` `any day` FALSE `any day` TRUE (`on` 20 4 2026) FALSE `any day` FALSE FALSE FALSE (`on` 21 4 2026) EQUALS `IN DEFAULT`
-- An "extension" to a day before the rules' own last day does not shorten the time.
#ASSERT `r 1117 -- is the defendant in default` TRUE (`on` 1 3 2026) `NO CONDITIONAL` `any day` FALSE `any day` TRUE (`on` 20 3 2026) FALSE `any day` FALSE FALSE FALSE (`on` 25 3 2026) EQUALS `NOT YET`
#ASSERT `r 1117 -- is the defendant in default` TRUE (`on` 1 3 2026) `NO CONDITIONAL` `any day` FALSE `any day` FALSE `any day` TRUE (`on` 20 3 2026) TRUE FALSE FALSE (`on` 10 4 2026) EQUALS `STRUCK OUT`
#ASSERT `r 1117 -- is the defendant in default` TRUE (`on` 1 3 2026) `NO CONDITIONAL` `any day` FALSE `any day` FALSE `any day` FALSE `any day` FALSE TRUE FALSE (`on` 10 4 2026) EQUALS `STAYED`
#ASSERT `r 1117 -- is the defendant in default` TRUE (`on` 1 3 2026) `NO CONDITIONAL` `any day` FALSE `any day` FALSE `any day` FALSE `any day` FALSE FALSE TRUE (`on` 10 4 2026) EQUALS `ACKNOWLEDGED`
#ASSERT `r 1117 -- is the defendant in default` FALSE (`on` 1 3 2026) `NO CONDITIONAL` `any day` FALSE `any day` FALSE `any day` FALSE `any day` FALSE FALSE FALSE (`on` 10 4 2026) EQUALS `NOT ORIGINATING CLAIM`
-- Served 10 December 2026: last day 15 January 2027 (the Christmas days not counted).
#ASSERT `r 1117 -- is the defendant in default` TRUE (`on` 10 12 2026) `NO CONDITIONAL` `any day` FALSE `any day` FALSE `any day` FALSE `any day` FALSE FALSE FALSE (`on` 15 1 2027) EQUALS `NOT YET`
#ASSERT `r 1117 -- is the defendant in default` TRUE (`on` 10 12 2026) `NO CONDITIONAL` `any day` FALSE `any day` FALSE `any day` FALSE `any day` FALSE FALSE FALSE (`on` 16 1 2027) EQUALS `IN DEFAULT`
-- Conditional notice lapsed (filed 5 March 2026): defence due 17 April 2026.
#ASSERT `r 1117 -- is the defendant in default` TRUE (`on` 1 3 2026) `CONDITIONAL LAPSED` (`on` 5 3 2026) FALSE `any day` FALSE `any day` FALSE `any day` FALSE FALSE FALSE (`on` 17 4 2026) EQUALS `NOT YET`
#ASSERT `r 1117 -- is the defendant in default` TRUE (`on` 1 3 2026) `CONDITIONAL LAPSED` (`on` 5 3 2026) FALSE `any day` FALSE `any day` FALSE `any day` FALSE FALSE FALSE (`on` 18 4 2026) EQUALS `IN DEFAULT`

