§ `r 1102 and schedule 3, part 3.1 -- the payment that stays a debt claim`

-- $9 999 in the Magistrates Court: 9 999 + 100 interest + 507 + 300 fees = 10 906.
#ASSERT `r 1102 -- what must the defendant pay to stay my debt claim` TRUE TRUE `MC` FALSE 9999 100 300 EQUALS JUST 10906
-- $10 000: the next band, 1 031: 10 000 + 1 031 + 300 = 11 331.
#ASSERT `r 1102 -- what must the defendant pay to stay my debt claim` TRUE TRUE `MC` FALSE 10000 0 300 EQUALS JUST 11331
-- $249 999: 249 999 + 1 538 = 251 537.
#ASSERT `r 1102 -- what must the defendant pay to stay my debt claim` TRUE TRUE `MC` FALSE 249999 0 0 EQUALS JUST 251537
-- $250 000 in the Magistrates Court falls in no band (finding 1).
#ASSERT `r 1102 -- what must the defendant pay to stay my debt claim` TRUE TRUE `MC` FALSE 250000 0 0 EQUALS NOTHING
-- Supreme Court, $400 000: 400 000 + 5 000 + 1 538 + 500 = 407 038.
#ASSERT `r 1102 -- what must the defendant pay to stay my debt claim` TRUE TRUE `SC` FALSE 400000 5000 500 EQUALS JUST 407038
-- Supreme Court, $30 000, could have been in the Magistrates Court: 30 000 + 1 232 = 31 232 (r 1102 (2)).
#ASSERT `r 1102 -- what must the defendant pay to stay my debt claim` TRUE TRUE `SC` TRUE 30000 0 0 EQUALS JUST 31232
#ASSERT `r 1102 -- what must the defendant pay to stay my debt claim` FALSE TRUE `MC` FALSE 9999 0 0 EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `r 1102 -- what must the defendant pay to stay my debt claim` TRUE FALSE `MC` FALSE 9999 0 0 EQUALS NOTHING

